MeasureA =
VAR SelectedOrder =
    SELECTEDVALUE ( 'MeasureA Field Parameter'[MeasureA Field Parameter Order] )
RETURN
    SWITCH (
        SelectedOrder,
        0, [Revenue Measure],
        1, [Units Sold Measure],
        2, [Customer Count Measure]
    )
// Optional pattern: making MeasureA (or MeasureB) swappable via a slicer,
// the same way Category is.
//
// Unlike Category, this is NOT required -- MeasureA/MeasureB are ordinary
// measures, so they can always be renamed-for-this-visual freely with no
// naming constraint. Use this pattern only if you specifically want a
// report viewer to swap which underlying measure feeds MeasureA at view
// time (e.g. toggling between Revenue / Units Sold / Customer Count).
//
// Unlike a field-parameter-driven Category, this measure itself keeps a
// perfectly normal, freely-renameable identity -- the field parameter here
// only selects which measure it evaluates internally, via SWITCH. DAX has
// no way to dynamically dereference "whichever measure is selected" without
// enumerating the candidates like this -- same static-reference constraint
// as Vega-Lite's own field bindings.
//
// Setup:
// 1) Create a SEPARATE field parameter (a distinct DAX object from the
//    MeasureA measure above -- Modeling -> New parameter -> Fields) over
//    your candidate measures, e.g. named "MeasureA Field Parameter":
//
//    MeasureA Field Parameter = {
//        ("Revenue", NAMEOF ( [Revenue Measure] ), 0),
//        ("Units Sold", NAMEOF ( [Units Sold Measure] ), 1),
//        ("Customer Count", NAMEOF ( [Customer Count Measure] ), 2)
//    }
//
// 2) Add a slicer bound to it.
//
// 3) The MeasureA measure above wraps that selection in a stably-named
//    measure -- THIS is what actually goes in the Values well as MeasureA.
